WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.387
A scalar subquery can also appear in the SELECT list.

00:00:04.387 --> 00:00:08.252
Here, the inner query calculates one overall average age.

00:00:08.252 --> 00:00:14.052
Because it is not correlated, the same value appears beside every patient row.

00:00:14.052 --> 00:00:18.887
This is useful when you want to show a row value and a benchmark together.

00:00:18.887 --> 00:00:24.097
Run the query and notice that the average does not change from patient to patient.

00:00:24.097 --> 00:00:28.167
A subquery has a contract: it returns a shape.

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:33.097
A scalar subquery must return at most one value where it is used.

00:00:33.097 --> 00:00:40.077
Before writing syntax, predict whether the inner query returns one value, one column with many rows,

00:00:40.077 --> 00:00:46.400
or a table. Shape mistakes are easier to prevent than to debug after the query becomes large.
